#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:3
msgid "Agent Panel"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:5
msgid ""
"The Agent Panel is where you interact with AI agents that can read, write, "
"and run code in your project. It's the core of Zed's AI code editing "
"experience — use it for code generation, refactoring, debugging, "
"documentation, and general questions."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:8
msgid ""
"Open it with `agent: new thread` from [the Command Palette](../getting-"
"started.md#command-palette) or click the ✨ icon in the status bar."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:10
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:12
msgid ""
"If you're using the Agent Panel for the first time, you need to have at "
"least one LLM provider or external agent configured. You can do that by:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:15
msgid ""
"[subscribing to our Pro plan](https://zed.dev/pricing), so you have access "
"to our hosted models"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:16
msgid ""
"[using your own API keys](./llm-providers.md#use-your-own-keys), either from "
"model providers like Anthropic or model gateways like OpenRouter."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:17
msgid ""
"using an [external agent](./external-agents.md) like [Gemini CLI](./external-"
"agents.md#gemini-cli) or [Claude Agent](./external-agents.md#claude-agent)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:19
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概覽"

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:21
msgid ""
"With an LLM provider or external agent configured, type in the message "
"editor and press `enter` to submit. Expand the editor with <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">shift-alt-escape\\|shift-alt-escape</kbd> if you need "
"more room."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:24
msgid ""
"Responses stream in with indicators showing [which tools](./tools.md) the "
"model is using. The sections below cover what you can do from here."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:27
msgid ""
"Note that for external agents, like [Gemini CLI](./external-agents.md#gemini-"
"cli) or [Claude Agent](./external-agents.md#claude-agent), some of the "
"features outlined below may _not_ be supported—for example, _restoring "
"threads from history_, _checkpoints_, _token usage display_, and others. "
"Their availability varies depending on the agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:30
msgid "Creating New Threads"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:32
msgid "By default, the Agent Panel uses Zed's first-party agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:34
msgid ""
"Start a new thread with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-t\\|ctrl-alt-t</"
"kbd>, or open the \"New Thread…\" menu via the `+` icon in the top-right of "
"the panel toolbar (in the empty state, this menu is exposed as the agent "
"selector button on the left). You can also open that menu with <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-shift-n\\|ctrl-alt-shift-n</kbd>."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:36
msgid "From the \"New Thread…\" menu you can:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:38
msgid ""
"Pick **Zed Agent** or any installed [external agent](./external-agents.md) "
"to start a new thread with that agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:39
msgid ""
"Choose **New From Summary** to start a fresh Zed Agent thread seeded with a "
"summary of the current conversation — useful for compacting long threads as "
"you approach the context window limit."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:41
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">agent: new external agent thread</code> creates another "
"thread with the currently selected agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:43
msgid ""
"You can also start a new thread from the [Threads Sidebar](./parallel-agents."
"md#threads-sidebar), scoped to a specific project — see [Running Multiple "
"Threads](./parallel-agents.md#running-multiple-threads)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:45
msgid "Managing Multiple Threads"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:47
msgid ""
"You can run multiple agent threads at once, each working independently with "
"its own agent, context window, and conversation history. Open the Threads "
"Sidebar with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-j\\|ctrl-alt-j</kbd> to see "
"all your threads grouped by project. Click any thread to switch to it, or "
"use the thread switcher (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-tab\\|ctrl-tab</"
"kbd>) to cycle between recent threads without opening the sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:49
msgid ""
"Threads you're no longer working on can be archived by hovering over them in "
"the sidebar and clicking the archive icon, or selecting them and pressing "
"<kbd class=\"keybinding\">shift-backspace\\|shift-backspace</kbd>. The "
"Thread History holds all your threads across all projects, sorted "
"chronologically, and you can restore them at any time."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:51
msgid ""
"If two threads might edit the same files, you can isolate one in a new Git "
"worktree. Use the worktree picker in the title bar to pick which worktree "
"the agent runs in, or create a new one. See [Worktree Isolation](./parallel-"
"agents.md#worktree-isolation) for details."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:53
msgid ""
"For more details on the Threads Sidebar and managing multiple projects, see "
"[Parallel Agents](./parallel-agents.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:55
msgid "Editing Messages"
msgstr "編輯訊息"

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:57
msgid ""
"Any message that you send to the model is editable. You can click on the "
"card that contains your message and re-submit it with an adjusted prompt and/"
"or new pieces of context."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:60
msgid "Queueing Messages"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:62
msgid ""
"Messages sent while the agent is in the generating state get, by default, "
"queued."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:64
msgid ""
"For the Zed agent, queued messages get sent at the next turn boundary, which "
"is usually between a tool call and a response, whereas for external agents, "
"the message gets sent at the end of the generation."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:66
msgid ""
"You can edit or remove (an individual or all) queued messages. You can also "
"still interrupt the agent immediately if you want by either clicking on the "
"stop button or by clicking the \"Send Now\" (double-enter) on a queued "
"message."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:69
msgid "Checkpoints"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:71
msgid ""
"Every time the model performs an edit, you should see a \"Restore "
"Checkpoint\" button at the top of your message, allowing you to return your "
"code base to the state it was in prior to that message."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:73
msgid ""
"The checkpoint button appears even if you interrupt the thread midway "
"through an edit, as this is likely a moment when you've identified that the "
"agent is not heading in the right direction and you want to revert back."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:75
msgid "Context Menu"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:77
msgid ""
"Right-click on any agent response in the thread view to access a context "
"menu with the following actions:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:79
msgid ""
"**Copy Selection**: Copies the currently selected text as Markdown "
"(available when text is selected)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:80
msgid ""
"**Copy This Agent Response**: Copies the full text of the agent response you "
"right-clicked on."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:81
msgid ""
"**Scroll to Top / Scroll to Bottom**: Scrolls to the beginning or end of the "
"thread, depending on your current position."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:82
msgid ""
"**Open Thread as Markdown**: Opens the entire thread as a Markdown file in a "
"new tab."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:84
msgid "Navigating the Thread"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:86
msgid ""
"In long conversations, use the scroll arrow buttons at the bottom of the "
"panel to jump to your most recent prompt or to the very beginning of the "
"thread. You can also scroll the thread using arrow keys, Page Up/Down, Home/"
"End, and Shift+Page Up/Down to jump between messages, when the thread pane "
"is focused."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:88
msgid ""
"When focus is in the message editor, you can also use <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-pageup\\|ctrl-pageup</kbd>, <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-pagedown\\|ctrl-pagedown</kbd>, <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-home\\|ctrl-home</kbd>, <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-end\\|ctrl-end</kbd>, <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-alt-up\\|ctrl-alt-up</kbd>, and <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-alt-down\\|ctrl-alt-down</kbd> to navigate the "
"thread, or <kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-alt-pageup\\|ctrl-alt-shift-"
"pageup</kbd> and <kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-alt-pagedown\\|ctrl-alt-"
"shift-pagedown</kbd> to jump between your prompts."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:90
msgid "Thread titles"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:92
msgid ""
"Thread titles are auto-generated based on the content of the conversation. "
"But you can also edit them manually by clicking the title and typing, or "
"regenerate them by clicking the \"Regenerate Thread Title\" button in the "
"ellipsis menu in the top right of the panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:95
msgid "Following the Agent"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:97
msgid ""
"Follow the agent as it reads and edits files by clicking the crosshair icon "
"at the bottom left of the panel. Your editor will jump to each file the "
"agent touches."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:100
msgid ""
"You can also hold `cmd`/`ctrl` when submitting a message to automatically "
"follow."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:102
msgid "Get Notified"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:104
msgid ""
"If you send a prompt to the Agent and then put Zed in the background, you "
"can choose to be notified when its generation wraps up via:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:106
msgid "a visual notification that appears in the top right of your screen"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:107
msgid "a sound notification"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:109
msgid ""
"These notifications can be used together or individually, and you can use "
"the `agent.notify_when_agent_waiting` and `agent.play_sound_when_agent_done` "
"settings keys to customize that, including turning both off entirely."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:111
msgid "Reviewing Changes"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:113
msgid ""
"Once the agent has made changes to your project, the panel will surface "
"which files, how many of them, and how many lines have been edited."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:115
msgid ""
"To see which files specifically have been edited, expand the accordion bar "
"that shows up right above the message editor or click the `Review Changes` "
"button (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">shift-ctrl-r\\|ctrl-shift-r</kbd>), which "
"opens a special multi-buffer tab with all changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:117
msgid ""
"You can accept or reject each individual change hunk, or the whole set of "
"changes made by the agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:119
msgid ""
"Edit diffs also appear in singleton buffers. If your active tab had edits "
"made by the AI, you'll see diffs with the same accept/reject controls as in "
"the multi-buffer. You can turn this off, though, through the `agent."
"single_file_review` setting."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:123
msgid "Adding Context"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:125
msgid ""
"The agent can search your codebase to find relevant context, but providing "
"it explicitly improves response quality and reduces latency."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:127
msgid ""
"Add context by typing `@` in the message editor. You can mention files, "
"directories, symbols, previous threads, rules files, and diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:130
msgid ""
"When you paste multi-line code selections copied from a buffer, Zed "
"automatically formats them as @-mentions with the file context. To paste "
"content without this automatic formatting, use <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-"
"shift-v\\|ctrl-shift-v</kbd> to paste raw text directly."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:133
msgid "Selection as Context"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:135
msgid ""
"Additionally, you can also select text in a buffer or terminal and add it as "
"context by using the <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd->\\|ctrl-></kbd> "
"keybinding, running the <code class=\"hljs\">agent: add selection to thread</"
"code> action, or choosing the \"Selection\" item in the `+` menu in the "
"message editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:137
msgid "Images as Context"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:139
msgid ""
"It's also possible to attach images in your prompt for providers that "
"support vision models. OpenAI GPT-4o and later, Anthropic Claude 3 and "
"later, Google Gemini 1.5 and 2.0, and Bedrock vision models (Claude 3+, "
"Amazon Nova Pro and Lite, Meta Llama 3.2 Vision, Mistral Pixtral) all "
"support image inputs."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:142
msgid ""
"To add an image, you can either search in your project's directory by @-"
"mentioning it, or drag it from your file system directly into the agent "
"panel message editor. Copying an image and pasting it is also supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:145
msgid "Token Usage"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:147
msgid ""
"Zed surfaces how many tokens you are consuming for your currently active "
"thread near the profile selector in the panel's message editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:149
msgid ""
"Once you approach the model's context window, a banner appears above the "
"message editor suggesting to start a new thread with the current one "
"summarized and added as context. You can also do this at any time with an "
"ongoing thread via the \"Agent Options\" menu on the top right, where you'll "
"see a \"New from Summary\" button, as well as simply @-mentioning a past "
"thread in a new one.."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:152
msgid "Changing Models"
msgstr "變更模型"

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:154
msgid ""
"After you've configured your LLM providers—either via [a custom API key](./"
"llm-providers.md) or through [Zed's hosted models](./models.md)—you can "
"switch between their models by clicking on the model selector on the message "
"editor or by using the <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-/\\|ctrl-alt-/</"
"kbd> keybinding."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:156
msgid ""
"The same model can be offered via multiple providers - for example, Claude "
"Sonnet 4.5 is available via Zed Pro, OpenRouter, Anthropic directly, and "
"more. Make sure you've selected the correct model **_provider_** for the "
"model you'd like to use, delineated by the logo to the left of the model in "
"the model selector."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:159
msgid "Favoriting Models"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:161
msgid ""
"You can mark specific models as favorites either through the model selector, "
"by clicking on the star icon button that appears as you hover the model, or "
"through your settings via the `agent.favorite_models` settings key."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:163
msgid ""
"Cycle through your favorites with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">alt-tab\\|alt-l</"
"kbd> without opening the model selector."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:165
msgid "Using Tools"
msgstr "使用工具"

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:167
msgid ""
"The Agent Panel supports tool calling, which enables agentic editing. Zed "
"includes several [built-in tools](./tools.md) for searching your codebase, "
"editing files, running terminal commands, and more."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:170
msgid ""
"You can also extend the set of available tools via [MCP Servers](./mcp.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:172
msgid "Profiles"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:174
msgid ""
"Profiles act as a way to group tools. Zed offers three built-in profiles and "
"you can create as many custom ones as you want."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:177
msgid "Built-in Profiles"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:179
msgid ""
"`Write`: A profile with tools to allow the LLM to write to your files and "
"run terminal commands. This one essentially has all built-in tools turned on."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:181
msgid ""
"`Ask`: A profile with read-only tools. Best for asking questions about your "
"code base without the concern of the agent making changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:183
msgid ""
"`Minimal`: A profile with no tools. Best for general conversations with the "
"LLM where no knowledge of your code base is necessary."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:186
msgid ""
"You can explore the exact tools enabled in each profile by clicking on the "
"profile selector button > `Configure` button > the one you want to check out."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:188
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can also use either the command palette, by running <code "
"class=\"hljs\">agent: manage profiles</code>, or the keybinding directly, "
"<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-p\\|ctrl-alt-p</kbd>, to have access to "
"the profile management modal."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:190
msgid ""
"Use <kbd class=\"keybinding\">shift-tab\\|shift-tab</kbd> to cycle through "
"available profiles without opening the modal."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:192
msgid "Custom Profiles"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:194
msgid ""
"You can also create a custom profile through the Agent Profile modal. From "
"there, you can choose to `Add New Profile` or fork an existing one with a "
"custom name and your preferred set of tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:197
msgid ""
"It's also possible to override built-in profiles. In the Agent Profile "
"modal, select a built-in profile, navigate to `Configure Tools`, and "
"rearrange the tools you'd like to keep or remove."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:200
msgid ""
"Zed will store this profile in your settings using the same profile name as "
"the default you overrode."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:202
msgid ""
"All custom profiles can be edited via the UI or by hand under the `agent."
"profiles` key in your settings file."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:204
msgid ""
"To delete a custom profile, open the Agent Profile modal, select the profile "
"you want to remove, and click the delete button."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:206
msgid "Tool Permissions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:208
msgid ""
"**Note:** In Zed v0.224.0 and above, tool approval is controlled by `agent."
"tool_permissions.default`. In earlier versions, it was controlled by the "
"`agent.always_allow_tool_actions` boolean (default `false`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:211
msgid ""
"Zed's Agent Panel provides the `agent.tool_permissions.default` setting to "
"control tool approval behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:213
msgid ""
"`\"confirm\"` (default) — Prompts for approval before running any tool action"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:214
msgid "`\"allow\"` — Auto-approves tool actions without prompting"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:215
msgid "`\"deny\"` — Blocks all tool actions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:217
msgid ""
"When the agent requests permission for an action, the confirmation menu "
"includes options to allow or deny once, plus \"Always for <tool>\" choices "
"that set a tool-level default. When Zed can extract a safe pattern from the "
"input, it also offers pattern-based \"Always for ...\" choices that add "
"`always_allow`/`always_deny` rules. MCP tools only support tool-level "
"defaults."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:221
msgid ""
"Even with `\"default\": \"allow\"`, per-tool `always_deny` and "
"`always_confirm` patterns are still respected — so you can auto-approve most "
"actions while blocking or gating specific ones."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:223
msgid ""
"Learn more about [how tool permissions work](./tool-permissions.md), how to "
"further customize them, and other details."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:225
msgid "Model Support"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:227
msgid ""
"Tool calling needs to be individually supported by each model and model "
"provider. Therefore, despite the presence of built-in tools, some models may "
"not have the ability to pick them up. You should see a \"No tools\" label if "
"you select a model that falls into this case."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:231
msgid ""
"All [Zed's hosted models](./models.md) support tool calling out-of-the-box."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:233
msgid "MCP Servers"
msgstr "MCP 伺服器"

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:235
msgid ""
"Similarly to the built-in tools, some models may not support all tools "
"included in a given MCP Server. Zed's UI will inform you about this via a "
"warning icon that appears close to the model selector."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:238
msgid "Errors and Debugging"
msgstr "錯誤與除錯"

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:240
msgid ""
"If you hit an error or unusual LLM behavior, open the thread as Markdown "
"with `agent: open thread as markdown` and attach it to your GitHub issue."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:242
msgid ""
"You can also open threads as Markdown by clicking on the file icon button, "
"to the right of the thumbs down button, when focused on the panel's editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:244
msgid "Feedback"
msgstr "意見反饋"

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:246
msgid ""
"You can rate agent responses to help improve Zed's system prompt and tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:248
msgid ""
"Note that rating responses will send your data related to that response to "
"Zed's servers. See [AI Improvement](./ai-improvement.md) and [Privacy and "
"Security](./privacy-and-security.md) for more information about Zed's "
"approach to AI improvement, privacy, and security. **_If you don't want data "
"persisted on Zed's servers, don't rate_**. We will not collect data for "
"improving our Agentic offering without you explicitly rating responses."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:253
msgid ""
"To help improve Zed's system prompt and tools, rate responses with the "
"thumbs up/down controls at the end of each response. In case of a thumbs "
"down, a new text area will show up where you can add more specifics about "
"what happened."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:256
msgid ""
"You can provide feedback on the thread at any point after the agent "
"responds, and multiple times within the same thread."
msgstr ""
